{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-04-Oct-2023-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Two mixtures A and B have the following compositions: Mixture A has copper and tin in a ratio of 1:2 Mixture B has copper and tin in a ratio of 1:3 If equal quantities of mixtures A and B are used for producing mixture C, then find the ratio of copper and tin in mixture C.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "If the volume of a sphere is 38808 cm3, then its surface area is:", "options": [{"text": "5554 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "5574 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "5564 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "5544 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The area of a rhombus having one side measuring 17 cm and one diagonal measuring 16 cm is:", "options": [{"text": "280 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "180 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "240 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "210 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "By selling 42 m of cloth, Vijay gains the selling price of 7 m of cloth. Find the profit percentage.", "options": [{"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Ramesh gives fifteen per cent additional discount along with a discount of 25% on the marked price of a sofa set. If the selling price of the sofa set is ₹12,750, then find the marked price of the sofa set.", "options": [{"text": "₹20,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹23,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹22,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹24,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "Two pipes can fill a cistern in 12 hours and 16 hours, respectively. The pipes are opened simultaneously and it is found that due to leakage at the bottom, it takes 90 minutes more to fill the cistern. How much time will the leakage take to empty the completely filled tank?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "leak", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A sum of money amounts to ₹1,200 in 2 years and becomes ₹1,260 in 3 years at compound interest, when interest is compounded annually. What is the rate of compound interest per annum?", "options": [{"text": "5%", "added": false}, {"text": "3%", "added": false}, {"text": "4%", "added": false}, {"text": "6%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Find the least value of 16cosec2θ + 25sin2θ.", "options": [{"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "21.68 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "22.75 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "26.23 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "25.76 percent", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "If cosec A + cot A = 3, 0 ≤ A ≤ 900 , then find the value of cosA. ⁡", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "36 equally efficient workers can paint 25 identical walls in 48 days. In how many days can 45 such workers paint 60 such walls?", "options": [{"text": "92.36", "added": false}, {"text": "92.16", "added": false}, {"text": "91.96", "added": false}, {"text": "91.16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Which of the following numbers leaves the remainder equal to the highest common factor of 6, 8 and 9, when divided by 6, 8 and 9?", "options": [{"text": "291", "added": false}, {"text": "575", "added": false}, {"text": "506", "added": false}, {"text": "433", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "remainder-based", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Simplify the given expression.", "options": [{"text": "6(1-x2)", "added": false}, {"text": "- 3(1-x2)", "added": false}, {"text": "- 6(1-x2)", "added": false}, {"text": "3(1-x2)", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5.5", "added": false}, {"text": "7.5", "added": false}, {"text": "7.0", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "The average weight of 49 students is 53 kg. When a new student is admitted to the class, the average decreases by 500 g. Find the weight of the new student.", "options": [{"text": "48 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "18 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "28 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "38 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "In an election between two candidates, the difference between the candidates who won and lost was 2,500 votes. The candidate who won got 75% of the votes, and there were no invalid votes. The total number of votes polled of the losing candidate was:", "options": [{"text": "1875", "added": false}, {"text": "5000", "added": false}, {"text": "1250", "added": false}, {"text": "3750", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "In an election between two candidates,30% of the electorate did not cast their votes. 20% of the votes polled were found invalid. The winning candidate got 64% of the valid votes and won by a majority of 3136 votes. Find the number of voters enrolled in the voter list.", "options": [{"text": "20000", "added": false}, {"text": "25000", "added": false}, {"text": "24000", "added": false}, {"text": "30000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Find the mean proportion of x3y and xy3.", "options": [{"text": "x2y2", "added": false}, {"text": "x3y3", "added": false}, {"text": "xy", "added": false}, {"text": "x4y4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "The least common multiple of 12, 18 and 27 is :", "options": [{"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "216", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "108", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "12 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "10 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "11 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "13 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "What is the smallest perfect square number which is completely divisible by 4, 6, 9, 12 and 15?", "options": [{"text": "784", "added": false}, {"text": "900", "added": false}, {"text": "961", "added": false}, {"text": "841", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "A vehicle is going at one-fourth of its usual speed and it takes an extra 45 minutes to reach its destination. Its usual time to cover the same distance is:", "options": [{"text": "15 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "10 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "30 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "20 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Kanchan lent ₹10,000 for 2 years and ₹5,000 for 4 years at the same rate of simple interest. If the total interest received by Kanchan is ₹2,000, then what was the rate of interest?", "options": [{"text": "5%", "added": false}, {"text": "2%", "added": false}, {"text": "3%", "added": false}, {"text": "4%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "The average weight of A, B and C is 77 kg. If the average weight of A and B is 68 kg and that of B and C is 83 kg, then the weight (in kg) of B is:", "options": [{"text": "74", "added": false}, {"text": "71", "added": false}, {"text": "73", "added": false}, {"text": "67", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "The diameter of a hemisphere is equal to the diagonal of a rectangle of length 4 cm and breadth 3 cm. Find the total surface area (in cm2) of the hemisphere.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "A cylindrical metallic rod of diameter 2 cm and length 45 cm is melted and converted into wire of uniform thickness and length 5 m. The diameter of the wire is:", "options": [{"text": "3 mm", "added": false}, {"text": "2 mm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 mm", "added": false}, {"text": "5 mm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "If the base radius and the height of a right circular cone are increased by 10%, then the percentage increase in the volume is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "The given pie chart shows the distribution of land under various food crops. The expenditure invested on these food crops is ₹25,000 per annum. Study the pie chart carefully and answer the question that follows. The expenditure invested in Rice and Barley is what percentage (correct to 2 decimal places) of the expenditure invested in Wheat and Bajra?", "options": [{"text": "206.55%", "added": false}, {"text": "206.66%", "added": false}, {"text": "260.66%", "added": false}, {"text": "260.55%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "If perimeter of the circle is 13.2 cm, then the radius of the circle is ____.", "options": [{"text": "6.6 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "4.2 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "2.1 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3.3 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "A goods train 350 m long passes through a tunnel of 1250m in 80 seconds. What is the speed of the train?", "options": [{"text": "72 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "64 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "78 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "56 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of employees in five different organisations A, B, C, D and E in different departments. Which department has a minimum number of employees in each organisation?", "options": [{"text": "Marketing", "added": false}, {"text": "Production", "added": false}, {"text": "Accounts", "added": false}, {"text": "Legal", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "−1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "In a triangle LMN, OP is a line segment drawn parallel to the side MN. OP intersects the sides LM and LN at O and P, respectively. If LM = 15 cm, OM = 4 cm, and PN = 5 cm, then what is the length (in cm) of the side LN?", "options": [{"text": "16.25", "added": false}, {"text": "18.75", "added": false}, {"text": "20.25", "added": false}, {"text": "22.75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "sec A - tanA ⁡", "added": false}, {"text": "cosec A + cotA ⁡", "added": false}, {"text": "sec A + tanA ⁡", "added": false}, {"text": "cosec A - cotA ⁡", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "Determine the LCM of two numbers if their HCF is 12 and their ratio is 13 : 15.", "options": [{"text": "1780", "added": false}, {"text": "2450", "added": false}, {"text": "1890", "added": false}, {"text": "2340", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "940", "added": false}, {"text": "960", "added": false}, {"text": "920", "added": false}, {"text": "880", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "Find the least number which when divided by 4, 9, 12 and 15, leaves the remainder 3 in each case.", "options": [{"text": "360", "added": false}, {"text": "183", "added": false}, {"text": "193", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5∶9", "added": false}, {"text": "3∶7", "added": false}, {"text": "5∶8", "added": false}, {"text": "3∶8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "On an item, there is an 18% discount on the marked price of ₹26,000. After giving an additional season’s discount, the item is sold at ₹16,000. How much was the season’s discount correct upto two places of decimal?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "In a ΔPQR,∠P=90°,∠R=47° and PS⊥QR. Find the value of ∠QPS.", "options": [{"text": "43°", "added": false}, {"text": "47°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}, {"text": "40°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "Sanjay and Rohan can complete a work in 8 days and 12 days, respectively. Starting with Sanjay, they work on alternate days. In how many days will the work be completed?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9,780", "added": false}, {"text": "9,880", "added": false}, {"text": "9,560", "added": false}, {"text": "9,950", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "AB is a chord of a circle having radius 1.7 cm. If the distance of this chord AB from the centre of the circle is 0.8 cm, then what is the length (in cm) of the chord AB?", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "12%", "added": false}, {"text": "8%", "added": false}, {"text": "4%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "If the HCF of 45 and 55 is expressible in the form of 55 × 5 + 45m, then what is the value of m?", "options": [{"text": "–6", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "–5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "The monthly salary of a person is ₹50,000. He spends 40% of his salary on household expenses, 25% on rent, and 15% on transportation, and saves the remaining amount. What is his yearly savings?", "options": [{"text": "₹1,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,10,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,20,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹90,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "The cost price of pulses is 12% less than the selling price. Using a faulty weighing machine, shopkeeper is able to earn 25% profit. How much per cent of the faulty machine shows more weight as compared to the actual weight (Rounded off to the nearest integer)?", "options": [{"text": "13%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "14%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}]}